{"kind":"article","identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/Performance"},"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The binary-size budget, the "},{"code":"Task","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" lifecycle guarantee, and the re-render characteristics of the default placeholders — what’s measured, what’s guaranteed, and why."}],"metadata":{"title":"Performance","roleHeading":"Article","role":"article","modules":[{"name":"ScreenStates"}]},"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates"]]},"schemaVersion":{"patch":0,"minor":3,"major":0},"sections":[],"seeAlsoSections":[{"anchor":"Related-Documentation","title":"Related Documentation","identifiers":["doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/ScreenStateStore","doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/ConcurrencyAndCancellation","doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/GettingStartedWithSwiftUI"]}],"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/screenstates\/performance"]}],"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"content","content":[{"type":"heading","text":"Overview","level":2,"anchor":"Overview"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"ScreenStates’ pitch is “small, dependency-free, drop into any screen.” This article covers the three ways that’s kept measurable rather than just assumed: a CI-enforced size budget, an audited concurrency guarantee, and a documented rendering characteristic."}]},{"type":"heading","text":"The binary-size budget","level":2,"anchor":"The-binary-size-budget"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"CI builds "},{"code":"swift build -c release","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" on every push and sums the resulting "},{"code":".o","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" sizes for the "},{"code":"ScreenStates","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" target, failing the build if that total exceeds the budget committed in "},{"code":".github\/binary-size-budget.json","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":". There’s no single linked artifact to measure instead — the library product is “automatic,” and nothing in the package’s own build graph links it standalone — so the "},{"code":".o","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" total is the closest deterministic proxy available."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A legitimate feature addition that grows this total past the budget isn’t blocked forever: bump "},{"code":"maxBytes","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" in that file as part of the same PR, the same way a dependency lockfile gets updated alongside the change that needed it. The job never bumps it on its own."}]},{"type":"heading","text":"The Task lifecycle guarantee","level":2,"anchor":"The-Task-lifecycle-guarantee"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/ScreenStateStore","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":"’s "},{"code":"load","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"\/"},{"code":"loadCollection","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"\/"},{"code":"refresh","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"\/"},{"code":"refreshCollection","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"\/"},{"code":"loadWithRetry","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" each store their running "},{"code":"Task","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" in a private "},{"code":"currentTask","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" property, read by "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/ScreenStateStore\/cancel()","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"code":"deinit","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":". Every one of those "},{"code":"Task","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"s captures "},{"code":"self","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" as "},{"code":"[weak self]","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", not strongly — audited specifically to rule out a "},{"code":"self -> currentTask -> closure -> self","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" retain cycle keeping a store alive after its last external reference is dropped."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"In practice, a completed "},{"code":"Task","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" releases its closure’s captures on return regardless of capture style, so this mostly matters for a still-"},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"running"}]},{"type":"text","text":" operation: without "},{"code":"[weak self]","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", a store couldn’t become eligible for deallocation until that operation finished, even once every other reference to it was already gone. See "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/ConcurrencyAndCancellation","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" for the rest of the "},{"code":"Task","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" lifecycle — cancellation, overlapping calls, and the automatic cancel-on-"},{"code":"deinit","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" safety net this guarantee supports."}]},{"type":"heading","text":"Re-render characteristics of the default placeholders","level":2,"anchor":"Re-render-characteristics-of-the-default-placeholders"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/ScreenStateStore\/isRefreshing","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/ScreenStateStore\/refreshError","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" only ever go active once "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/ScreenStateStore\/refresh(_:)","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":"\/"},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/ScreenStateStore\/refreshCollection(_:)","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" have confirmed "},{"code":"state","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" is already "},{"code":".data","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" — both fall back to "},{"code":"load(_:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"\/"},{"code":"loadCollection(_:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" otherwise, which never touch either property. That means "},{"code":"isRefreshing","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"\/"},{"code":"refreshError","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" can never be observed alongside "},{"code":".empty","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"code":".loading","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", or "},{"code":".error","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", so none of the three default placeholders can ever be on screen mid-refresh."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A parent view that reads "},{"code":"store.state","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" (via "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/ScreenStateView","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":") and "},{"code":"store.isRefreshing","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"\/"},{"code":"refreshError","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" in the same "},{"code":"body","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" — the pattern "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/GettingStartedWithSwiftUI","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" uses for a refresh toast — still has its "},{"code":"body","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" re-evaluated whenever either changes, same as any "},{"code":"@Observable","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" property read in a SwiftUI "},{"code":"body","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":". This guarantee is about "},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"which"}]},{"type":"text","text":" placeholder that re-evaluation could ever affect, not about avoiding the re-evaluation itself: since a default placeholder is only ever on screen while "},{"code":"isRefreshing","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"\/"},{"code":"refreshError","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" are both inactive, that re-evaluation never has a placeholder to needlessly re-render in the first place — only whatever renders the "},{"code":".data","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" case could be affected."}]}]}],"references":{"doc://screenstates.ScreenStates/documentation/ScreenStates/ScreenState":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/ScreenState","url":"\/documentation\/screenstates\/screenstate","type":"topic","role":"symbol","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"enum"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"ScreenState"}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The four canonical states of a screen: nothing to show yet, in flight,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"showing data, or failed."}],"title":"ScreenState","kind":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"ScreenState"}]},"doc://screenstates.ScreenStates/documentation/ScreenStates/ScreenStateStore/load(_:)":{"title":"load(_:)","type":"topic","kind":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"load","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"(","kind":"text"},{"text":"@Sendable","kind":"attribute"},{"text":" () ","kind":"text"},{"text":"async","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"throws","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" -> ","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:12ScreenStates0A10